ies\nWebcams\nOffices, Services, Resources\nFormation\nAthletics\nGlobal\nAgora Portal\nEmergency\nJobs at BC\nLibraries\nBookstore\nMaps & Directions\nHours\nEvents\nBC Dining\nClose\nHome\nGraduate\nTuition, Stipend, & Health Care\nGraduate\nPh.D. Program\nTuition, Stipend, & Health Care\nForms & Resources\nInternational Students\nRecent Ph.D. Graduates\nTuition, Stipend, & Health Care\nTuition & Stipend\nThe Graduate School of the Morrissey College of Arts and Sciences Biology Department covers tuition and health care for all active Ph.D. students up to six years in exchange for service to the department. Ph.D. students are responsible to pay the Graduate Student Activity Fee.\nPh.D. students receive an annual service stipend as compensation for 20 hours of departmental service each week as a Teaching Assistant or Research Assistant.\nInsurance/Health Care\nAll BC students must have health insurance. For students who don't carry a policy of their own, Boston College is required by law to provide access to a health insurance policy. All Ph.D. registered for a course(s) and receiving a on full-stipend are covered under University Medical Insurance.\nStudent Medical Insurance\nUniversity Health Services\nBack To Top\nBiology Department\n355 Higgins Hall\n617-552-3540\nMorrissey College of Arts and Sciences\nGasson Hall\n140 Commonwealth Avenue\nChestnut Hill, MA 02467\nContact\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nDepartments\nArt, Art History, and Film\nBiology\nChemistry\nClassical Studies\nCommunication\nComputer Science\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nEconomics\nEngineering\nEnglish\nGerman Studies\nHistory\nMathematics\nMusic\nPhilosophy\nPhysics\nPolitical Science\nPsychology\nRomance Languages and Literatures\nSlavic & Eastern Languages and Literatures\nSociology\nTheatre\nTheology\nGiving to Morrissey\nGive to Biology\nApply\nUndergraduate\nGraduate\nFollow Us\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYoutube\nAccessibility\nLegal\nEmergency\nNotice of Nondiscrimination\nCopyright \u